  "releaseNotes": "1.2.0: RetrievalChunk<TRecord> — a strongly typed chunk whose Record is the source record (TRecord) instead of an untyped dictionary, so callers read chunk.Record.Id rather than chunk.Record[\"Id\"]. It derives from the unchanged non-generic RetrievalChunk, which keeps the supplementary dictionary the record-agnostic processors read by key. RetrievalResults stays non-generic: IList<T> is invariant, so a typed Chunks view could only be a stale copy — cast the chunks with chunks.Cast<RetrievalChunk<TRecord>>() instead.",
